WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.780
We sometimes find ourselves and newish

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:02.790
 

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.730
professional settings or social

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:04.740
 

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.010
situations where we're not exactly sure

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:07.020
 

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.410
how to contribute, what we should be

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:09.420
 

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.900
prioritizing. So let's talk about the top

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:11.910
 

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.459
three priorities that you should have

00:00:13.459 --> 00:00:13.469
 

00:00:13.469 --> 00:00:16.169
when you're in this new or novel situation.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:17.520
 

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.060
I'm Alex Lyon and I'm here to

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:22.080
 

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.720
provide professional development tips to

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:23.730
 

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.029
help you increase your impact and lead

00:00:26.029 --> 00:00:26.039
 

00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:28.790
your teams with more excellence. If you

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:28.800
 

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.410
have never subscribed to this channel

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:30.420
 

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.740
before, I'd like to invite you to do so. I

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:33.750
 

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.229
think all these videos help people that

00:00:36.229 --> 00:00:36.239
 

00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:38.299
I call rising leaders. If you're a team

00:00:38.299 --> 00:00:38.309
 

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:40.910
leader, front-line supervisor, or front-

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:40.920
 

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.130
line manager, everything on here is meant

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:43.140
 

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.410
to help you sharpen your skills. So go

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:45.420
 

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.840
ahead and subscribe, thumbs up the video,

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:47.850
 

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.540
if you like it, start commenting in the

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:50.550
 

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.979
section below. I'm really good about

00:00:51.979 --> 00:00:51.989
 

00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:53.569
responding to almost every single

00:00:53.569 --> 00:00:53.579
 

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:56.219
comment people post so we can start a dialogue.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.340
Okay. Now on to the lesson. I don't know

00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:58.350
 

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.950
about you but a lot of times I feel like

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:00.960
 

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.340
my old moves at my old team might not

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:04.350
 

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.280
translate to a new setting. So now with

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:07.290
 

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.960
higher-level people or people I don't

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:08.970
 

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.850
know that well and I'm not really sure

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:10.860
 

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.040
how to jump in and contribute in a meaningful way.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.280
Let's talk about three ways that you can

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:16.290
 

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.770
instantly position yourself as a

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:18.780
 

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.990
credible contributor to that group.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:21.000
 

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.320
Number one. Open a communication channel.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:24.330
 

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.170
That means non-verbally and verbally

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:27.180
 

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.469
open a line of communication to every

00:01:30.469 --> 00:01:30.479
 

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:32.870
other single person in that room. So

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:32.880
 

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.819
let's just picture a room and several

00:01:34.819 --> 00:01:34.829
 

00:01:34.829 --> 00:01:37.010
other people and you walk into this

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:37.020
 

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.980
situation, you should instantly attempt

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:39.990
 

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.140
to make eye contact with every other

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:42.150
 

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:45.620
person in the room. You also verbally

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:45.630
 

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.810
want to say something to each person if

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:47.820
 

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.240
you can fit appropriate. Minimally, the

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:50.250
 

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.560
people next to you but certainly

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:51.570
 

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.289
everybody if this is pre-meeting, if

00:01:54.289 --> 00:01:54.299
 

00:01:54.299 --> 00:01:56.090
you're making small talk. So you open a

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:56.100
 

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.520
nonverbal and a verbal channel. If there's,

00:01:58.520 --> 00:01:58.530
 

00:01:58.530 --> 00:01:59.810
if it's appropriate and there's someone

00:01:59.810 --> 00:01:59.820
 

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.310
there close enough to you shake their

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:01.320
 

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.630
hand especially if it's before the

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:02.640
 

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.830
meeting is starting,

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:03.840
 

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.240
especially if you're just introducing

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:05.250
 

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:08.690
yourself. Most, most places are still okay

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:08.700
 

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.460
with handshakes. I know a lot of places,

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:10.470
 

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:13.100
like. Don't touch. It's not Okay to touch.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:13.110
 

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:14.240
But a handshake is still considered

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:14.250
 

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.370
appropriate and professional. And then

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:16.380
 

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.780
maintain, during the course of that

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:17.790
 

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.550
meeting, and continue to make eye contact,

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:19.560
 

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.910
continue to orient your body toward

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:22.920
 

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.560
people. You don't want to fall into the

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:24.570
 

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.110
trap of looking down at your computer or

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:27.120
 

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.120
your devices the entire time.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:29.130
 

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:30.680
In fact, I have a whole separate video

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:30.690
 

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:33.860
about the downside of using devices in

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:33.870
 

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.660
meetings. I encourage you to watch that

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:35.670
 

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.790
I'll put a link in the description below

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:37.800
 

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.370
this video to that. So that's the first

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:40.380
 

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.840
step is opening a channel and

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:41.850
 

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.730
maintaining that channel the entire

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:43.740
 

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.860
meeting. The second step is to learn

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:45.870
 

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:48.230
every person's name. When I know

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:48.240
 

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.690
someone's name, I feel really equipped to

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:50.700
 

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.370
have a conversation with them because I

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:52.380
 

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.540
know who they are,

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:53.550
 

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.370
hopefully they know who I am, and now at

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:55.380
 

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.350
least you have a way to refer to that

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:57.360
 

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.540
person. You know their identity. So what I

00:02:59.540 --> 00:02:59.550
 

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:01.130
like to do is I sit down to these

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:01.140
 

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.530
meetings especially in a new situation. I

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:03.540
 

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.690
take out an old-fashioned piece of paper

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:05.700
 

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.370
and write down everyone's name. A lot of

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:07.380
 

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.020
time people will introduce themselves,

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:09.030
 

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:11.690
for example, and as they go around, I make

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:11.700
 

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.120
notes about who's who. And that way,

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:14.130
 

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.949
throughout the meeting I can look at my

00:03:15.949 --> 00:03:15.959
 

00:03:15.959 --> 00:03:18.050
notes. And if I have a little down moment

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:18.060
 

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.910
where I'm not doing anything that's too

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:19.920
 

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.220
hard, I look down the list and I look at

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:22.230
 

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.050
their faces and I rehearse their names

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:24.060
 

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.090
in my head to really make sure I

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:26.100
 

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.580
engrain those names and own those names

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:28.590
 

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.380
by the end of that meeting and I really have

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:30.390
 

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.060
memorized everybody in the room.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:32.070
 

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.470
It's really not that hard if you put

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:33.480
 

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.150
just a little bit of effort into it. So

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:35.160
 

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.009
now you know everybody's name. The third

00:03:37.009 --> 00:03:37.019
 

00:03:37.019 --> 00:03:39.979
step to contributing is to make sure you

00:03:39.979 --> 00:03:39.989
 

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:43.550
add some kind of value to that meeting. You

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:43.560
 

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.729
don't just want to listen, although listening

00:03:46.729 --> 00:03:46.739
 

00:03:46.739 --> 00:03:47.330
is good.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:47.340
 

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:48.740
You don't just want to be non-verbally

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:48.750
 

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.630
involved, although nonverbals are good.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:50.640
 

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.120
You want to do things like offer your

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:53.130
 

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:55.910
opinion at least once or twice. Offer

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:55.920
 

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.310
some information. Ask a question that

00:03:58.310 --> 00:03:58.320
 

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.870
leads the group in a positive direction.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:03:59.880
 

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.870
Build on something that somebody else

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:02.880
 

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.360
has said. That's a really easy way to get

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:05.370
 

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.100
involved. You want to make sure you say

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:07.110
 

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:09.259
something. If you're at that meeting, you

00:04:09.259 --> 00:04:09.269
 

00:04:09.269 --> 00:04:11.600
have to realize, even if your brand new,

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:11.610
 

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:14.750
people expect you to contribute and say

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:14.760
 

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.000
something of value from the very first

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:17.010
 

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:19.250
meeting. You can't just sit around and

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:19.260
 

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:20.960
ramp up over the course of two, three,

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:20.970
 

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.520
four meetings. They want you contributing

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:22.530
 

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:23.930
right away.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:23.940
 

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:26.430
In fact, I said something really useless.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:26.440
 

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.990
In fact, it was a little confrontational

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:28.000
 

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.300
at a meeting once among some very high-

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:30.310
 

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.550
level people. And I felt kind of

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:32.560
 

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:33.930
embarrassed and I clammed up. And

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:33.940
 

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.580
afterwards, I said to my boss, I'm really

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:35.590
 

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:38.280
sorry that I said that. That was stupid. I

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:38.290
 

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.570
should have thought about my words more

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:39.580
 

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.340
carefully. He put his hand on my shoulder

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:41.350
 

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:43.080
and said, Alex, at least you said

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:43.090
 

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:44.790
something. Otherwise we're all going to

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:44.800
 

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.740
start wondering what you were paying,

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:46.750
 

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.690
we were paying you for. I thought, wow

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:48.700
 

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.490
that's a pretty graceful response. But,

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:50.500
 

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.140
even at that level, people want you

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:52.150
 

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.090
contributing. They want you from the very

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:54.100
 

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.860
first meeting to say something where you

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:55.870
 

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:57.990
add value. So don't be shy about it. Break

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:58.000
 

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.920
the ice. Contribute verbally something. So

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:01.930
 

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.420
those are the three ways that you can

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:03.430
 

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:06.270
prioritize your work in these meetings

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:06.280
 

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.370
And it is work. You have to go in with a

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:08.380
 

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:10.320
little bit of a plan into these meetings

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:10.330
 

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.900
so you show up as a professional, as

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:12.910
 

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.820
someone who is credible, as someone who

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:14.830
 

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.010
should be taken seriously by the other

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:17.020
 

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:19.440
people in the group. So I mentioned

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:19.450
 

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:21.300
earlier if you haven't yet subscribed, I

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:21.310
 

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:23.550
encourage you to do so. I encourage you

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:23.560
 

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:25.230
to look around the channel, find some

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:25.240
 

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:28.050
other videos that might help you move

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:28.060
 

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.760
your career forward, help you move your

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:29.770
 

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:31.500
team forward, and I look forward to

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:31.510
 

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:33.690
starting a conversation in the comments

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:33.700
 

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.090
section below this and other videos. So

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:36.100
 

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.590
thanks. God bless and I hope you get to

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:37.600
 

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.630
use the tips we are talking about your very

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:39.640
 

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:45.780
next team meeting.

